      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "St Pancras, especially around the Eurostar area, can feel like a sprawling, bustling maze, much like a large, busy underground network. It's not entirely straightforward, but it's manageable if you keep your bearings, which is easier than trying to navigate a truly chaotic, tiny space. I'd suggest having your ticket and knowing your platform number *before* you arrive, so you don't have to panic looking for information.\n\nIt's a big transit hub, so while there are plenty of people, the main paths to the international departure areas are usually well-signposted. Don't let the sheer volume of people overwhelm you; just focus on following the clear signs for \"Eurostar\" or \"International Departure.\" If you get confused, look for staff members—they are usually helpful, though sometimes they are busy themselves!",
      "source": "target",
